#!/opt/homebrew/bin/python3
"""bin/seal-check -- PREREG-v2 §13: what the tree may hold at the draft tag, at the seal, and at v2's day 28.

    bin/seal-check                 the seal: §13 (a)-(e), on main after the switch, before `git tag -a prereg-v2-seal`
    bin/seal-check --draft         before `git tag -a prereg-v2-draft` on the build branch (§13's draft command)
    bin/seal-check --since TAG     v2's `make results` (loop/inference_v2.py runs it with prereg-v2-seal): §13's allowlist
                                   from the seal until T0_v2 + 28 d
    bin/seal-check --at REV        the seal's verdict replayed on the commit REV names (v2's make results runs it with
                                   prereg-v2-seal and RESULTS-v2 §0 prints it, §13): (a), (c), (d), (§12) and (§2) on
                                   REV's tree, the seal's time REV's tagger date; (b) and (e) judged the working tree
                                   at the seal and are not run

Exit 0 when every check passes, 1 when one fails (each check on its own line, PASS or FAIL, then the verdict), 2 on a
usage error or when git cannot answer. It checks the git tree this file lives in (as bin/promote does) and writes
nothing there: the listed deviations are taken out in a temporary index outside the tree. It sends nothing.

The seal (no flag) exits 0 only when all of §13's five hold:
(a) `git merge-base --is-ancestor refs/tags/prereg-v2-draft HEAD`;
(b) `git status --porcelain` is empty;
(c) `git diff -U0 refs/tags/prereg-v2-draft HEAD -- . ':(exclude)RESULTS.md' ':(exclude)HANDOFF.md' ':(exclude)proposals'
    ':(exclude)data/exclusions.tsv'` (printed in full; renames off, so a moved file is a deletion and an addition) has
    hunks only where §13 (c) allows them. The commits named in the first column of ERRATA.md's "v2 deviations" table (a
    heading holding those words; a row whose first cell is not a commit is refused), each one in prereg-v2-draft..HEAD
    (made after the tag, on the build or on main, where §13 has main take a fix only as a listed deviation until switch
    step (6), merged at step (4)) and not a merge, are taken out first: each one's diff
    applied in reverse to HEAD's tree, newest first, in a temporary index; a deviation that a later commit overlaps
    cannot be taken out, and (c) fails. Each is printed with its own diff. What is left is judged file by file:
    - PREREG-v2.md: every hunk replaces lines one for one, each a line of §12 (from `## 12.` to the next `## `) that
      holds ________ at the draft tag, by the same line with its blanks filled (each ________ replaced by text with no
      backtick or line break; a blank may stay a blank); §12's `Tables rebuilt at the switch:` line only as below;
    - prompts/v2.table.<p>.json and §12's rebuild line, under §8's once-only rebuild rule: either no v2 table differs
      from the draft tag's and the rebuild line, if filled, reads `no`; or the table of every p in config.PRODUCTS
      differs, all changed by one commit after the tag and no other, each reads as prompts.table reads it (v2, its
      product, prompts/v2.json's sha, the product's 81 states, buy, sell or hold), each answered by a model_answered
      other than the draft tag's table's (§8: rebuilt only when a different Jev version answers), and the rebuild line is
      filled and names that model_answered and each table's sha (prompts.table's canonical sha, the row's table_sha:
      its first 12 hex digits or more);
    - prompts/CURRENT: any hunk (its value is (d));
    - prompts/v<N>.json with N >= 3: added after the tag (v1's bin/promote) and not the version CURRENT names;
    - ERRATA.md: pure additions at the end (HEAD's text begins with the tag's whole text, which ends in a line break);
    - tests/test_frozen.py: every hunk replaces lines one for one, each line a pin whose key is PREREG-v2.md or
      prompts/v2.table.<p>.json for p in config.PRODUCTS (`"<path>": "<sha256>"`, the form STEPS §10.4 keeps them in;
      a line that only mentions one is not its pin), each pair differing only in that sha;
    - any other path: none.
    A listed deviation that touches a file holding what §13 says voids the draft tag (at_cadence, replay/paired,
    inference, the pooling or exclusion readers, rule_c, the alphabet or its cuts, PROMPT.md v2, the digest, promote's
    schedule) is named on a READ line (VOIDING: PREREG-v2.md and SPEC.md, which define them, and every file that holds
    or feeds them, loop/prompts.py's schedule, loop/report.py's days_table and loop/outcomes.py's t + h join included):
    a file is coarser than what it holds, so the reading is the author's;
(d) prompts/CURRENT names v2 (prompts.named);
(§12) §12 of PREREG-v2.md in HEAD is filled: no ________ left in it, and its T0_v2 and fee tiers read as loop.dash reads
    them for bin/promote, the report, status, the dash and v2's make results (a malformed field raises there). Not one of
    (a)-(e), but the seal's own precondition: the header has prereg-v2-seal made "once §12's fields are filled, tagged
    only after bin/seal-check exits 0", §13 seals "once §12 is filled", and after the tag --since refuses any edit of
    PREREG-v2.md, so a field left blank or unreadable at the seal could never be filled;
(§2) once §12's T_first_v2 and T0_v2 are read: T0_v2 is the first minute boundary >= T_first_v2 + 86,400 s (§2), or a
    re-derivation (§13: the seal was not made before that boundary, and T0_v2 is the first minute boundary >= the commit
    time of the fix that lets bin/seal-check pass + 86,400 s: a commit in prereg-v2-draft..HEAD made at or after the
    first boundary must give it; it is printed as RE-DERIVED); the seal, now, falls in [T_first_v2, T0_v2) (§2, §13:
    before the first v2 sample row); and T_first_v2 is the logs': the latest, over config.PRODUCTS, of each product's
    first live row (mode live, absence null) carrying the sha of HEAD's SPEC.md, read from the tree's data/ in
    config.store's layout (loop.dash.first_v2_rows, STEPS §10.6's rule; a product with no such row fails). Not one of
    (a)-(e) either: without it a stale, past or mistyped T0_v2 passed and moved every reader's window (2026-09-29 review);
    (c) also prints `git diff --stat` of the paths it excludes (RESULTS.md, HANDOFF.md, proposals, data/exclusions.tsv),
    which §13 has RESULTS-v2 §0 print beside the full diff;
(e) `make test` exits 0 in the tree (its last lines are printed). NOT RUN when (a)-(d), (§12) or (§2) already failed:
    the verdict is FAIL either way, and the suite takes minutes. (c) is NOT RUN without a draft tag on HEAD.

--draft exits 0 only when all of §13's three hold:
- no ________ remains in PREREG-v2.md outside §12, nor the other unwritten forms its pre-tag fields take (§1's `__` of 81
  state counts, §2's and §1's `<P2>`/`<P3>` product placeholders): searched in the header and §0-§11, where §1, §2, §3
  and §8 write their values before the tag; §13 names the token in its own text and §14 is the amendment log, so neither
  holds a field;
- probe/<D>/ is in HEAD with run.json naming D and its candidates (every p in config.PRODUCTS but SOL-USD among them),
  volume.json and <c>.jsonl for every candidate c run.json names (§2: the probe's rows are committed verbatim, not only
  the chosen products'), D the day §2 names in bold (`**D = YYYY-MM-DD**`; if §14 moves D, §2's D moves with it);
- D stands by bin/probe's own day verdict on those rows (its read_rows, transport_failed and day_verdict, as `bin/probe
  summarize` reads them): a void D "becomes the next UTC day, once, named in §14", so a §14 entry that moves D while §2
  still names the void day is refused here rather than passed on the void day's directory;
- §2's pre-tag fields are what the tree runs: its Products line is config.PRODUCTS (loop.dash.read_products_v2, in
  order), and its `TICK_p` and `Atoms (a10, a90)` fields give each added product config.TICK_P's value and
  config.LIQ_ATOMS's two numbers;
- prompts/v2.table.<p>.json is in HEAD for every p in config.PRODUCTS and reads as prompts.table reads it;
- PREREG-v2.md in HEAD is the tag prereg-v2-doc's, or §14 no longer reads "(none yet)" (no such tag: refused, since
  nothing can be compared).
The clean tree is the draft command's own `test -z "$(git status --porcelain)"`, before this.

--since TAG exits 0 only when TAG names a commit that is an ancestor of HEAD and `git diff -U0 TAG` (every tracked file as
it is on disk against TAG, so a change not yet committed is judged too; printed in full) touches only §13's post-seal
allowlist: prompts/v<N>.json and prompts/v<N>.table.<p>.json with N >= 3 and p in config.PRODUCTS, each added since TAG
(bin/promote's commits: promote writes a version's files new and never overwrites one, so one TAG holds stays as
sealed), prompts/CURRENT, HANDOFF.md, proposals/, data/exclusions-v2.tsv and data/looks.tsv. Untracked files are named on
a NOTE line and not judged (RESULTS-v2.md is one until it is committed).
"""
import argparse, datetime, hashlib, importlib.machinery, importlib.util, json, os, re, subprocess, sys, tempfile, time

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
REPO = os.path.dirname(HERE)
sys.path.insert(0, REPO)
from loop import config, dash, prompts                          # noqa: E402

DRAFT_TAG = "refs/tags/prereg-v2-draft"
DOC_TAG = "refs/tags/prereg-v2-doc"
PREREG = "PREREG-v2.md"
ERRATA = "ERRATA.md"
FROZEN_TEST = "tests/test_frozen.py"
CURRENT = "prompts/CURRENT"
EXCLUDED = ("RESULTS.md", "HANDOFF.md", "proposals", "data/exclusions.tsv")      # §13 (c)'s excludes, in its order
PATHSPEC = ("--", ".") + tuple(f":(exclude){p}" for p in EXCLUDED)
DIFF = ("diff", "-U0", "--no-color", "--no-ext-diff", "--no-textconv", "--no-renames")
BLANK = "________"
UNWRITTEN = re.compile(r"________|`_{2,}`|`<P\d+>`")   # --draft: a blank, §1's `__` counts, the `<P2>`/`<P3>` placeholders
REBUILD_LINE = "Tables rebuilt at the switch:"
NO_FIELD_SECTIONS = ("12", "13", "14")      # --draft: §12 keeps its blanks, §13 names the token, §14 is the log
PROBE_DAY_RE = re.compile(r"\*\*D = (\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})\*\*")
S2_TICKS = re.compile(r"`TICK_p`:\s*(.*?)\.\s+Atoms \(a10, a90\):\s*(.*?)\.(?:\s|$)", re.S)   # §2's two field runs
S2_PAIR = re.compile(r"`([^`\n]*)`\s*`([^`\n]*)`")                                       # `<product>` `<value>`
DEVIATIONS_RE = re.compile(r"^(#{1,6}) .*\bv2 deviations\b", re.I)
COMMIT_CELL = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{7,40}")
PRODUCT_NAME = re.compile(r"[A-Z0-9]{2,12}-[A-Z]{3,5}")      # a run.json candidate, joined into a path (bin/probe's form)
HEX12 = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{12,64}")
PIN_LINE = re.compile(r'^(\s*"(?:PREREG-v2\.md|prompts/v2\.table\.([^"/\s]+)\.json)"\s*:\s*")([0-9a-f]{64})(".*)$')
HUNK = re.compile(r"^@@ -(\d+)(?:,(\d+))? \+(\d+)(?:,(\d+))? @@")
VERSION_FILE = re.compile(r"^prompts/v(\d+)\.json$")
VERSION_TABLE = re.compile(r"^prompts/v(\d+)\.table\.(.+)\.json$")
SINCE_FILES = ("prompts/CURRENT", "HANDOFF.md", "data/exclusions-v2.tsv", "data/looks.tsv")   # §13, after the seal
SINCE_DIRS = ("proposals/",)
VOIDING = {                                 # §13: a deviation touching what these files hold voids the draft tag
    PREREG: "the text that defines every one of them (the alphabet and its cuts, inference, the pooling, the exclusion"
            " rule, promote's schedule)",
    "SPEC.md": "the alphabet and its cuts, the labels and fee columns replay and paired read",
    "loop/book.py": "at_cadence, replay, paired", "loop/outcomes.py": "the t + h join and the labels replay and paired read",
    "loop/report.py": "days_table (stop rule 3's table, which the exclusion readers' recompute reads) and the pairs",
    "loop/inference_v2.py": "inference and the pooling", "loop/inference.py": "inference",
    "loop/exclusions_v2.py": "an exclusion reader", "loop/exclusions.py": "an exclusion reader",
    "loop/state.py": "rule_c, the alphabet and its cuts",
    "loop/config.py": "the cuts (TICK_P, LIQ_ATOMS, LIQ_THIN_FALLBACK)",
    "loop/prompts.py": "current and activation, which enforce promote's schedule on every tick",
    "nightly/PROMPT.md": "PROMPT.md v2", "nightly/digest.py": "the digest", "bin/promote": "promote's schedule",
}
MAKE_TIMEOUT_S = 3600
TAIL_LINES = 4
DAY_S = 86400


def _now():
    """The seal's clock (epoch seconds): the time the seal is judged at, which §2 puts in [T_first_v2, T0_v2)."""
    return time.time()



class GitError(RuntimeError):
    pass


def _git(repo, *args, env=None, data=None, check=True):
    """git in `repo`, bytes in and out (a diff may hold any bytes); GitError on a non-zero exit when `check`."""
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-c", "core.quotepath=false", *args], cwd=repo, capture_output=True, env=env, input=data)
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        raise GitError(f"git {' '.join(args)}: exit {r.returncode}: {r.stderr.decode('utf-8', 'replace').strip()}")
    return r


def _text(b):
    return b.decode("utf-8", "replace")


def blob(repo, rev, path):
    """The file at `rev` (a commit or a tree), as text, or None when it is not there."""
    r = _git(repo, "cat-file", "blob", f"{rev}:{path}", check=False)
    return _text(r.stdout) if r.returncode == 0 else None


def hunks(diff):
    """The hunks of one file's -U0 diff: {"old", "old_n", "new", "new_n", "minus", "plus", "eof"}."""
    out, cur = [], None
    for line in diff.split("\n"):
        m = HUNK.match(line)
        if m:
            cur = {"old": int(m[1]), "old_n": int(m[2] if m[2] is not None else 1), "new": int(m[3]),
                   "new_n": int(m[4] if m[4] is not None else 1), "minus": [], "plus": [], "eof": False}
            out.append(cur)
        elif cur is not None and line[:1] == "-":
            cur["minus"].append(line[1:])
        elif cur is not None and line[:1] == "+":
            cur["plus"].append(line[1:])
        elif cur is not None and line[:1] == "\\":
            cur["eof"] = True                                    # "\ No newline at end of file"
    return out


def _at(h):
    return f"@@ -{h['old']},{h['old_n']} +{h['new']},{h['new_n']} @@"


def section_labels(lines):
    """Per line, its PREREG section: 'head' before `## 0.`, then 'N' from each `## N.` to the next."""
    labels, cur = [], "head"
    for line in lines:
        m = re.match(r"^## (\d+)\.", line)
        if m:
            cur = m.group(1)
        labels.append(cur)
    return labels


def section(text, n):
    m = re.search(rf"^## {n}\..*?(?=^## |\Z)", text, re.M | re.S)
    return m.group(0) if m else ""


def fills(old, new):
    """The values `new` puts in `old`'s blanks (each ________ replaced by text with no backtick or line break), or
    None when `new` is not `old` with its blanks filled."""
    parts = old.split(BLANK)
    if len(parts) < 2:
        return None
    m = re.fullmatch("([^`\n]+)".join(re.escape(p) for p in parts), new)
    return list(m.groups()) if m else None


def _blank(v):
    return re.fullmatch(r"_*", v.strip()) is not None


# ---- (c): the listed deviations, taken out in a temporary index -------------------------------------------------------
def deviations(repo, errata_text, rev="HEAD"):
    """(the commits ERRATA.md's "v2 deviations" table names, full shas, newest first; refusals). A row whose first cell
    is not a commit, a commit that is not in DRAFT_TAG..HEAD, and a merge commit are refused. DRAFT_TAG..HEAD, not the
    tag's descendants: from the draft tag until switch step (6) main takes a fix only as a listed deviation (§13), and
    such a commit, merged at switch step (4), is one HEAD reaches and the tag does not, with no tag below it."""
    order = _text(_git(repo, "rev-list", "--topo-order", f"{DRAFT_TAG}..{rev}").stdout).split()
    listed, bad, depth = [], [], None
    for line in errata_text.splitlines():
        h = re.match(r"^(#{1,6}) ", line)
        if h:
            m = DEVIATIONS_RE.match(line)
            depth = len(m.group(1)) if m else (None if depth is None or len(h.group(1)) <= depth else depth)
            continue
        if depth is None or not line.startswith("|"):
            continue
        cells = [c.strip() for c in line.strip().strip("|").split("|")]
        first = cells[0].strip("` ")
        if set(first) <= set("-: ") or first.lower() in ("commit", "sha"):
            continue                                             # the header and its separator
        if not COMMIT_CELL.fullmatch(first):
            bad.append(f"ERRATA.md's v2 deviations row {line.strip()[:80]!r} names no commit in its first cell (a row under"
                       " that heading is a deviation until the next heading of its level: other additions go under one)")
            continue
        r = _git(repo, "rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"{first}^{{commit}}", check=False)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            bad.append(f"ERRATA.md's v2 deviations row names {first}, which is not a commit here")
            continue
        sha = _text(r.stdout).strip()
        if sha not in order:
            bad.append(f"ERRATA.md's v2 deviations row names {sha[:12]}, which is not in prereg-v2-draft..HEAD (a commit "
                       "HEAD reaches and the draft tag does not: made after the tag, on the build or on main)")
            continue
        if len(_text(_git(repo, "rev-list", "--parents", "-n", "1", sha).stdout).split()) != 2:
            bad.append(f"ERRATA.md's v2 deviations row names {sha[:12]}, a merge: a deviation is one commit of its own")
            continue
        if sha not in listed:
            listed.append(sha)
    return sorted(listed, key=order.index), bad


def without(repo, commits, rev="HEAD"):
    """(`rev`'s tree with each commit's diff applied in reverse, newest first; refusals). Built in a temporary index:
    neither the tree nor the repository's index is touched."""
    if not commits:
        return _text(_git(repo, "rev-parse", f"{rev}^{{tree}}").stdout).strip(), []
    bad = []
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
        env = dict(os.environ, GIT_INDEX_FILE=os.path.join(d, "index"))
        _git(repo, "read-tree", rev, env=env)
        for c in commits:
            patch = _git(repo, "diff", "--binary", "--full-index", "--no-renames", "--no-color", "--no-ext-diff",
                         "--no-textconv", f"{c}^", c, *PATHSPEC).stdout
            if not patch.strip():
                continue
            r = _git(repo, "apply", "--cached", "-R", "--whitespace=nowarn", env=env, data=patch, check=False)
            if r.returncode != 0:
                bad.append(f"the listed deviation {c[:12]} cannot be taken out of HEAD (a later commit changed its lines;"
                           f" git apply -R: {_text(r.stderr).strip().splitlines()[-1] if r.stderr.strip() else 'failed'})")
        tree = _text(_git(repo, "write-tree", env=env).stdout).strip()
    return tree, bad


def changed(repo, a, b=None, pathspec=PATHSPEC):
    """[(status letter, path)] of `git diff --name-status` from a to b (b None: the files on disk)."""
    raw = _text(_git(repo, "diff", "--name-status", "--no-renames", "-z", a, *((b,) if b else ()), *pathspec).stdout)
    parts = [p for p in raw.split("\0")]
    return [(parts[i][:1], parts[i + 1]) for i in range(0, len(parts) - 1, 2) if parts[i]]


# ---- (c): the file-by-file rules ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def tables(repo, tree, products, paths, rev="HEAD"):
    """§8's once-only rebuild of v2's tables: (refusals, {"changed": [p], "models": {model}, "shas": {p: sha}})."""
    names = {p: f"prompts/v2.table.{p}.json" for p in products}
    info = {"changed": [p for p in products if names[p] in paths], "models": set(), "shas": {}}
    bad = []
    if not info["changed"]:
        return bad, info
    commits = _text(_git(repo, "rev-list", f"{DRAFT_TAG}..{rev}", "--", *names.values()).stdout).split()
    if len(commits) != 1:
        bad.append(f"prompts/v2.table.*.json: changed by {len(commits)} commits after prereg-v2-draft "
                   f"({', '.join(c[:12] for c in commits) or 'none on HEAD'}): §8 rebuilds them once, in one commit")
    missing = [p for p in products if p not in info["changed"]]
    if missing:
        bad.append(f"prompts/v2.table.*.json: {', '.join(info['changed'])} rebuilt and {', '.join(missing)} not: §8 "
                   "rebuilds every product's table together, once")
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as root:
        with open(os.path.join(root, "v2.json"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(blob(repo, tree, "prompts/v2.json") or "")
        for p in info["changed"]:
            text = blob(repo, tree, names[p])
            if text is None:
                bad.append(f"{names[p]}: removed after prereg-v2-draft")
                continue
            with open(os.path.join(root, f"v2.table.{p}.json"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                fh.write(text)
            try:
                t = prompts.table("v2", p, root)
            except prompts.PromptError as e:
                bad.append(f"{names[p]}: not a v2 table as prompts.table reads one: {e}")
                continue
            model = json.loads(text).get("model_answered")
            old = blob(repo, DRAFT_TAG, names[p])
            try:
                old_model = json.loads(old).get("model_answered") if old is not None else None
            except (ValueError, AttributeError):
                old_model = None
            if model == old_model:
                bad.append(f"{names[p]}: answered by {model!r}, the model the draft tag's table names: §8 rebuilds the"
                           " tables only when a different Jev version answers")
            info["models"].add(model)
            info["shas"][p] = t["sha"]
    return bad, info


def rebuild_value(value, info):
    """None when §12's rebuild line may hold `value` under §8's rule (info from tables()), else why not."""
    v = value.strip()
    if not info["changed"]:
        return None if v == "no" else f"§12's rebuild line reads {v!r} while no v2 table differs from the draft tag's: it may read only `no`"
    runs = HEX12.findall(v)
    missing = [str(m) for m in sorted(info["models"], key=str) if not isinstance(m, str) or m not in v]
    missing += [f"{p}'s table sha {s[:12]}" for p, s in info["shas"].items() if not any(s.startswith(h) for h in runs)]
    return (f"§12's rebuild line {v!r} does not name {', '.join(missing)} (§8: the answering Jev version and one sha per"
            " product)") if missing else None


def judge_prereg(draft_text, new_text, hs, info):
    """PREREG-v2.md's hunks: §12's blank fields filled, the rebuild line under §8's rule; and a rebuild recorded."""
    lines, bad = draft_text.split("\n"), []
    labels = section_labels(lines)
    for h in hs:
        where = f"{PREREG} {_at(h)}"
        if h["old_n"] != h["new_n"] or h["old_n"] == 0 or h["eof"]:
            bad.append(f"{where}: not a one-for-one replacement of lines (only §12's blank fields may be filled)")
            continue
        for i, (o, n) in enumerate(zip(h["minus"], h["plus"])):
            k = h["old"] - 1 + i
            if k >= len(lines) or lines[k] != o or labels[k] != "12" or BLANK not in o:
                bad.append(f"{where}: line {k + 1} {o[:70]!r} is not a blank field of §12")
                break
            vals = fills(o, n)
            if vals is None:
                bad.append(f"{where}: line {k + 1} changes beyond its blanks: {o!r} -> {n!r}")
                break
            if o.startswith(REBUILD_LINE):
                why = rebuild_value(vals[0], info)
                if why:
                    bad.append(f"{where}: {why}")
    if info["changed"]:
        line = next((l for l in section(new_text, 12).splitlines() if l.startswith(REBUILD_LINE)), None)
        vals = fills(next((l for l in section(draft_text, 12).splitlines() if l.startswith(REBUILD_LINE)), ""), line or "")
        if line is None or not vals or _blank(vals[0]):
            bad.append(f"{PREREG}: v2's tables were rebuilt and §12's rebuild line does not record it (§8, §12)")
    return bad


def judge_errata(draft_text, new_text):
    if draft_text and not draft_text.endswith("\n"):
        return [f"{ERRATA}: the draft tag's text does not end in a line break, so nothing can be added after it unchanged"]
    return [] if new_text.startswith(draft_text) else [f"{ERRATA}: a hunk that is not a pure addition at the end"]


def judge_frozen(hs, products):
    """tests/test_frozen.py's hunks: each line a pin whose KEY is PREREG-v2.md or a product's v2 table, only its sha
    changed; a line that merely mentions one (a comment, another file's pin) stays as the draft tag has it."""
    def pin(line):
        m = PIN_LINE.match(line)
        return m if m and (m.group(2) is None or m.group(2) in products) else None

    def same_pin(o, n):
        mo, mn = pin(o), pin(n)
        return bool(mo and mn) and (mo.group(1), mo.group(4)) == (mn.group(1), mn.group(4))

    bad = []
    for h in hs:
        if h["old_n"] != h["new_n"] or h["old_n"] == 0 or not all(same_pin(o, n) for o, n in zip(h["minus"], h["plus"])):
            bad.append(f"{FROZEN_TEST} {_at(h)}: a change beyond the sha of a pin of PREREG-v2.md or of v2's tables")
    return bad


def section12_unfilled(text):
    """Why §12 of `text` (PREREG-v2.md) is not filled, one reason a line; empty when it is: no ________ left, and
    T_first_v2, T0_v2 and the fee tiers read by loop.dash's readers (None there is a blank or a missing field; ValueError a malformed one).
    Returns (reasons, what was read)."""
    why, n = [], section(text, 12).count(BLANK)
    if n:
        why.append(f"{PREREG} §12 still holds {n} {BLANK} (the seal is made once §12 is filled; after it, --since refuses"
                   f" any edit of {PREREG})")
    read = {}
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
        path = os.path.join(d, PREREG)
        with open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(text)
        for name, reader in (("T_first_v2", dash.read_t_first_v2), ("T0_v2", dash.read_t0_v2),
                             ("fee tiers", dash.read_fee_tiers)):
            try:
                read[name] = reader(path)
            except ValueError as e:
                why.append(str(e))
                continue
            if read[name] is None:
                why.append(f"{PREREG} §12's {name} is blank or absent, as loop.dash reads it")
    return why, read


def _tick(epoch):
    return time.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M00Z", time.gmtime(epoch))


def _stamp(epoch):
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(epoch))


def _minute_up(epoch):
    """The first minute boundary at or after `epoch` (§2's T0_v2 rule, §13's re-derivation)."""
    return int(-(-epoch // 60) * 60)


def log_paths(repo, products):
    """Each product's decision log in `repo` in config.store's layout (data/decisions.jsonl for config.PRODUCT,
    data/<PRODUCT>/decisions.jsonl for the others): the logs of the tree checked, not of the code's own tree."""
    return {p: os.path.join(repo, "data", "decisions.jsonl") if p == config.PRODUCT else
            os.path.join(repo, "data", p, "decisions.jsonl") for p in products}


def times(repo, rev, read, sealed_at, products):
    """§2 and §13 on §12's two times, once both read: (refusals, lines). T0_v2 is the first minute boundary >= T_first_v2
    + 86,400 s, or a re-derivation (§13: the seal was not made before that; T0_v2 is then the first minute boundary >=
    the commit time of the fix that lets bin/seal-check pass + 86,400 s, which a commit in prereg-v2-draft..rev made at or
    after the first T0_v2 must give); the seal, made at `sealed_at`, falls in [T_first_v2, T0_v2); and T_first_v2 is the
    logs': the latest, over products, of each product's first live row carrying the sha of `rev`'s SPEC.md (§2; read
    from `repo`'s data/, as STEPS §10.6 computes it)."""
    tf, t0 = read.get("T_first_v2"), read.get("T0_v2")
    if tf is None or t0 is None:
        return [], []
    bad, lines = [], []
    first = _minute_up(tf + DAY_S)
    if t0 == first:
        lines.append(f"T0_v2 {_tick(t0)} is the first minute boundary >= T_first_v2 {_tick(tf)} + 86,400 s: not re-derived")
    elif t0 < first:
        bad.append(f"T0_v2 {_tick(t0)} is before {_tick(first)}, the first minute boundary >= T_first_v2 {_tick(tf)} + 86,400 s (§2)")
    else:
        found = None
        for line in _text(_git(repo, "log", "--format=%H %ct", f"{DRAFT_TAG}..{rev}", check=False).stdout).splitlines():
            parts = line.split()
            if len(parts) == 2 and parts[1].isdigit():
                ct = int(parts[1])
                if ct >= first and _minute_up(ct + DAY_S) == t0:
                    found = (parts[0], ct)
                    break
        if found is None:
            bad.append(f"T0_v2 {_tick(t0)} is neither {_tick(first)} (the first minute boundary >= T_first_v2 {_tick(tf)} +"
                       " 86,400 s, §2) nor a re-derivation (§13: the first minute boundary >= the commit time + 86,400 s of a"
                       f" commit in prereg-v2-draft..{rev} made at or after {_tick(first)})")
        else:
            lines.append(f"T0_v2 RE-DERIVED (§13; RESULTS-v2 §0 lists it): the seal was not made before {_tick(first)} (T_first_v2"
                         f" {_tick(tf)} + 86,400 s); T0_v2 {_tick(t0)} is the first minute boundary >= commit"
                         f" {found[0][:12]}'s time {_stamp(found[1])} + 86,400 s")
    if not tf <= sealed_at < t0:
        bad.append(f"the seal at {_stamp(sealed_at)} is not in [T_first_v2 {_tick(tf)}, T0_v2 {_tick(t0)}) (§2, §13: sealed before"
                   " the first v2 sample row)")
    else:
        lines.append(f"the seal at {_stamp(sealed_at)} is in [T_first_v2, T0_v2) (§2)")
    spec = _git(repo, "cat-file", "blob", f"{rev}:SPEC.md", check=False)
    if spec.returncode != 0:
        bad.append(f"SPEC.md is not in {rev}: T_first_v2 cannot be read from the logs (§2: the draft tree's spec_sha)")
        return bad, lines
    sha = hashlib.sha256(spec.stdout).hexdigest()
    paths = log_paths(repo, products)
    first_rows = dash.first_v2_rows(paths, sha)
    none = [p for p in products if first_rows[p] is None]
    if none:
        bad.append("no live row carrying SPEC.md's sha " + sha[:12] + "... in " + ", ".join(
            f"{p}'s log {os.path.relpath(paths[p], repo)}" for p in none) + ": T_first_v2 cannot be read from the logs (§2)")
    else:
        latest = max(first_rows.values())
        who = ", ".join(f"{p} {_tick(first_rows[p])}" for p in products)
        if latest != tf:
            bad.append(f"§12's T_first_v2 {_tick(tf)} is not the logs' {_tick(latest)} (each product's first live row carrying"
                       f" SPEC.md's sha {sha[:12]}...: {who}; §2: the latest of them)")
        else:
            lines.append(f"T_first_v2 {_tick(tf)} is the logs' (each product's first live row carrying SPEC.md's sha"
                         f" {sha[:12]}...: {who})")
    return bad, lines


def seal_time(repo, at):
    """When the seal was made, for --at: the tagger date of the annotated tag `at` names, else its commit's committer
    date."""
    r = _git(repo, "cat-file", "-t", at, check=False)
    if _text(r.stdout).strip() == "tag":
        for line in _text(_git(repo, "cat-file", "tag", at).stdout).splitlines():
            m = re.match(r"^tagger .* (\d+) [+-]\d{4}$", line)
            if m:
                return int(m.group(1))
            if not line:
                break
    return int(_text(_git(repo, "log", "-1", "--format=%ct", f"{at}^{{commit}}").stdout).strip())


def current_name(repo, rev):
    text = blob(repo, rev, CURRENT)
    names = [l.strip() for l in (text or "").splitlines() if l.strip()]
    return names[0] if len(names) == 1 else None


def judge(repo, tree, products, rev="HEAD"):
    """§13 (c) on DRAFT_TAG -> tree (`rev`'s, the listed deviations taken out): the refusals, one line each."""
    names = changed(repo, DRAFT_TAG, tree)
    paths = {p for _, p in names}
    bad, info = tables(repo, tree, products, paths, rev)
    table_paths = {f"prompts/v2.table.{p}.json" for p in products}
    cur = current_name(repo, rev)
    for status, path in names:
        d = _text(_git(repo, *DIFF, DRAFT_TAG, tree, "--", path).stdout)
        if path == PREREG:
            bad += judge_prereg(blob(repo, DRAFT_TAG, path) or "", blob(repo, tree, path) or "", hunks(d), info)
        elif path in table_paths or path == CURRENT:
            continue                                             # the rebuild rule above; CURRENT's value is (d)
        elif VERSION_FILE.match(path) and int(VERSION_FILE.match(path).group(1)) >= 3:
            n = VERSION_FILE.match(path).group(1)
            if status != "A":
                bad.append(f"{path}: {'changed' if status == 'M' else 'removed'} after prereg-v2-draft: only a version "
                           "file v1's bin/promote adds is allowed")
            elif cur == f"v{n}":
                bad.append(f"{path}: added after prereg-v2-draft and named by prompts/CURRENT")
        elif path == ERRATA:
            bad += judge_errata(blob(repo, DRAFT_TAG, path) or "", blob(repo, tree, path) or "")
        elif path == FROZEN_TEST:
            bad += judge_frozen(hunks(d), products)
        else:
            bad.append(f"{path}: {'added' if status == 'A' else 'removed' if status == 'D' else 'changed'} after "
                       "prereg-v2-draft, which §13 (c) does not allow")
    if info["changed"] and PREREG not in paths:
        bad.append(f"{PREREG}: v2's tables were rebuilt and §12's rebuild line does not record it (§8, §12)")
    return bad


def section2_config(text, products):
    """--draft: why §2's pre-tag fields (Products, TICK_p, atoms) are not what config holds, one reason a line; empty when
    they are. The tree tests, pins and runs config.PRODUCTS, config.TICK_P and config.LIQ_ATOMS; §2 writes the probe's
    choice before the tag; nothing else held the two to each other (2026-09-29 lens-5 review: §2 naming DOGE and AVAX
    passed with config holding ETH and XRP)."""
    why = []
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
        path = os.path.join(d, PREREG)
        with open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(text)
        try:
            named = dash.read_products_v2(path)
        except ValueError as e:
            return [str(e)]
    if named is None:
        return [f"§2's Products line still holds a blank"]
    if tuple(named) != tuple(products):
        why.append(f"§2's Products line names {', '.join(named)}; config.PRODUCTS is {', '.join(products)}")
    m = S2_TICKS.search(" ".join(section(text, 2).split()))
    ticks, atoms = ({a: b.strip() for a, b in S2_PAIR.findall(m.group(1))},
                    {a: b.strip() for a, b in S2_PAIR.findall(m.group(2))}) if m else ({}, {})
    for p in products:
        if p == config.PRODUCT:
            continue
        t, a = ticks.get(p), atoms.get(p)
        try:
            ok_t = t is not None and float(t) == config.TICK_P.get(p)
        except ValueError:
            ok_t = False
        if not ok_t:
            why.append(f"§2's TICK_p for {p} is {t!r}; config.TICK_P holds {config.TICK_P.get(p)!r}")
        nums = tuple(int(x) for x in re.findall(r"\d+", a or ""))
        if nums != tuple(config.LIQ_ATOMS.get(p) or ()):
            why.append(f"§2's atoms (a10, a90) for {p} are {a!r}; config.LIQ_ATOMS holds {config.LIQ_ATOMS.get(p)!r}")
    return why


def _probe_tool():
    """bin/probe as a module, for its day verdict (no bytecode written beside it; its run and volume lock, never taken
    here, are what a running probe holds)."""
    path = os.path.join(HERE, "probe")
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("probe_tool", path)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader("probe_tool", loader))
    before, sys.dont_write_bytecode = sys.dont_write_bytecode, True
    try:
        loader.exec_module(mod)
    finally:
        sys.dont_write_bytecode = before
    return mod


def probe_void(repo, d, day, candidates):
    """bin/probe summarize's day verdict on HEAD's `d`/ (PREREG-v2 §2): the reasons D is void, empty when it stands.
    Each candidate's rows are read from HEAD, as its read_rows reads a file, and judged by its day_verdict."""
    probe = _probe_tool()
    read = []
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as t:
        for c in candidates:
            path = os.path.join(t, f"{c}.jsonl")
            with open(path, "wb") as fh:
                fh.write(_git(repo, "cat-file", "blob", f"HEAD:{d}/{c}.jsonl", check=False).stdout)
            read.append(probe.read_rows(path, day)[0])
    minutes = len({r["tick_id"] for rows in read for r in rows})
    transport = sum(1 for rows in read for r in rows if probe.transport_failed(r))
    return probe.day_verdict(minutes, transport, len(candidates))


# ---- the three modes -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def _say(out, line=""):
    out.write(line + "\n")
    out.flush()


def _verbatim(out, title, diff):
    _say(out, title)
    for line in diff.splitlines():
        _say(out, "    | " + line)
    if not diff.strip():
        _say(out, "    (empty)")


def seal(repo, products, out, at=None):
    """§13's (a)-(e) and the seal's own two (§12, §2) on HEAD and the working tree; with `at` (--at REV) the same
    judgement replayed on the commit REV names, as v2's make results prints it in RESULTS-v2 §0: (b) and (e), which
    judged the working tree at the seal, are not run, (d) reads REV's prompts/CURRENT, and the seal's time is REV's
    tagger date (an annotated tag) or its commit's committer date."""
    fails = []
    rev = "HEAD" if at is None else _text(_git(repo, "rev-parse", "--verify", f"{at}^{{commit}}").stdout).strip()
    name = "HEAD" if at is None else at

    def verdict(tag, ok, text):
        _say(out, f"({tag}) {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'}: {text}")
        if not ok:
            fails.append(tag)

    r = _git(repo, "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", DRAFT_TAG, rev, check=False)
    verdict("a", r.returncode == 0, f"{DRAFT_TAG} is an ancestor of {name}" if r.returncode == 0 else
            f"`git merge-base --is-ancestor {DRAFT_TAG} {name}` exited {r.returncode}"
            + (f": {_text(r.stderr).strip()}" if r.stderr.strip() else ""))
    if at is None:
        st = _text(_git(repo, "status", "--porcelain").stdout)
        verdict("b", not st.strip(), "`git status --porcelain` is empty" if not st.strip() else
                f"`git status --porcelain` lists {len(st.splitlines())}: " + "; ".join(l.strip() for l in st.splitlines()[:5]))
    else:
        _say(out, f"(b) NOT RUN: --at judges the commit {at} names ({rev}), not a working tree; the seal ran it on its own")
    if "a" in fails:
        _say(out, f"(c) NOT RUN: there is no draft tag on {name} to diff from")
    else:
        cmd = f"git diff -U0 {DRAFT_TAG} {name} -- . " + " ".join(f"':(exclude){p}'" for p in EXCLUDED)
        _verbatim(out, f"(c) `{cmd}` (renames off), verbatim:",
                  _text(_git(repo, *DIFF, DRAFT_TAG, rev, *PATHSPEC).stdout))
        _verbatim(out, f"(c) the paths it excludes, `git diff --stat {DRAFT_TAG} {name} -- {' '.join(EXCLUDED)}` (§13), verbatim:",
                  _text(_git(repo, "diff", "--stat", "--no-color", "--no-renames", DRAFT_TAG, rev, "--", *EXCLUDED).stdout))
        listed, bad = deviations(repo, blob(repo, rev, ERRATA) or "", rev)
        for c in listed:
            _verbatim(out, f"(c) listed deviation {c} (ERRATA.md's v2 deviations table), taken out before the judgement:",
                      _text(_git(repo, "show", "-U0", "--no-color", "--no-ext-diff", "--no-textconv", "--no-renames",
                                 "--format=%H %s", c).stdout))
            for _, path in changed(repo, f"{c}^", c):
                if path in VOIDING:
                    _say(out, f"(c) READ: the listed deviation {c[:12]} touches {path}, which holds {VOIDING[path]}: a "
                              "deviation touching those voids the draft tag (§13), which a file alone cannot show")
        tree, more = without(repo, listed, rev)
        bad += more
        if not more:
            bad += judge(repo, tree, products, rev)
        verdict("c", not bad, f"every hunk is one §13 (c) allows ({len(listed)} listed deviation(s) taken out)" if not bad
                else f"{len(bad)} hunk(s) or file(s) §13 (c) does not allow:")
        for b in bad:
            _say(out, "    " + b)
    if at is None:
        try:
            cur = prompts.named(os.path.join(repo, "prompts"))
        except prompts.PromptError as e:
            cur, why = None, str(e)
    else:
        cur, why = current_name(repo, rev), f"{CURRENT} in {at} names no one version"
    verdict("d", cur == "v2", "prompts/CURRENT names v2" if cur == "v2" else
            f"prompts/CURRENT names {cur!r}, not v2" if cur else f"prompts/CURRENT cannot be read: {why}")
    why, read = section12_unfilled(blob(repo, rev, PREREG) or "")
    tf, t0 = read.get("T_first_v2"), read.get("T0_v2")
    verdict("§12", not why, f"{PREREG} §12 is filled: no {BLANK} left, T_first_v2 {_tick(tf) if tf is not None else '?'},"
            f" T0_v2 {_tick(t0) if t0 is not None else '?'} and "
            f"{len((read.get('fee tiers') or {}).get('tiers', []))} fee tier(s) read as loop.dash reads them" if not why
            else "; ".join(why))
    if tf is None or t0 is None:
        _say(out, "(§2) NOT RUN: §12's T_first_v2 or T0_v2 is not read (above)")
    else:
        bad2, lines2 = times(repo, rev, read, _now() if at is None else seal_time(repo, at), products)
        for line in lines2:
            _say(out, "(§2) " + line)
        verdict("§2", not bad2, "T0_v2 from T_first_v2, the seal inside [T_first_v2, T0_v2) and T_first_v2 from the logs"
                if not bad2 else "; ".join(bad2))
    if at is not None:
        _say(out, "(e) NOT RUN: --at judges a commit; the seal ran `make test` on its own tree")
    elif fails:
        _say(out, f"(e) NOT RUN: ({'), ('.join(fails)}) failed already, and the suite takes minutes")
    else:
        env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if not k.startswith("MAKE")}
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(["make", "test"], cwd=repo, capture_output=True, env=env, timeout=MAKE_TIMEOUT_S)
            rc, tail = r.returncode, _text(r.stdout + r.stderr).strip().splitlines()[-TAIL_LINES:]
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            rc, tail = None, [f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}"]
        verdict("e", rc == 0, f"`make test` exited {rc}; its last lines:")
        for line in tail:
            _say(out, "    | " + line)
    return fails


def draft(repo, products, out):
    fails = []

    def verdict(tag, ok, text):
        _say(out, f"{tag}: {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'}: {text}")
        if not ok:
            fails.append(tag)

    text = blob(repo, "HEAD", PREREG)
    if text is None:
        verdict("blanks", False, f"{PREREG} is not in HEAD")
        text = ""
    else:
        lines = text.split("\n")
        labels = section_labels(lines)
        left = [f"line {i + 1} (§{labels[i]})" if labels[i] != "head" else f"line {i + 1} (the header)"
                for i, l in enumerate(lines) if UNWRITTEN.search(l) and labels[i] not in NO_FIELD_SECTIONS]
        verdict("blanks", not left, f"no {BLANK}, `__` or `<P2>`/`<P3>` outside §12 (searched: the header and §0-§11; §13"
                " names the token and §14 is the amendment log)" if not left else
                f"{BLANK}, `__` or `<P2>`/`<P3>` remains outside §12 at " + ", ".join(left))
    why2 = section2_config(text, products)
    verdict("§2", not why2, "§2's Products, TICK_p and atoms are config.PRODUCTS, config.TICK_P and config.LIQ_ATOMS"
            if not why2 else "; ".join(why2))
    m = PROBE_DAY_RE.search(section(text, 2))
    if m is None:
        verdict("probe", False, f"§2 of {PREREG} names no day as **D = YYYY-MM-DD**")
    else:
        day = m.group(1)
        d = f"probe/{day}"
        have = set(_text(_git(repo, "ls-tree", "--name-only", "HEAD", d + "/").stdout).splitlines())
        try:
            run = json.loads(blob(repo, "HEAD", f"{d}/run.json") or "null")
        except ValueError:
            run = None
        run = run if isinstance(run, dict) else {}
        cands = run.get("candidates")
        if not (isinstance(cands, list) and cands and all(isinstance(c, str) and PRODUCT_NAME.fullmatch(c) for c in cands)):
            cands = None
        chosen = [p for p in products if p != config.PRODUCT]
        want = ["run.json", "volume.json"] + [f"{c}.jsonl" for c in (cands or chosen)]
        gone = [f for f in want if f"{d}/{f}" not in have]
        never = [p for p in chosen if cands is not None and p not in cands]
        why = (f"{d}/ lacks {', '.join(gone)} in HEAD (§2: the probe's rows are committed verbatim, every candidate's)"
               if gone else f"{d}/run.json names day {run.get('day')!r}, not {day}" if run.get("day") != day
               else f"{d}/run.json names no candidates (a list of product names, as bin/probe writes it)" if cands is None
               else f"{d}/run.json's candidates do not include {', '.join(never)}: a product the probe never ran"
               if never else None)
        verdict("probe", why is None, f"{d}/ is in HEAD with {', '.join(want)}" if why is None else why)
        if why is None:
            void = probe_void(repo, d, day, cands)
            verdict("D", not void, f"{d}/'s rows: D stands by bin/probe's day verdict (rows in >= 95 % of D's minutes,"
                    " transport failures <= 5 % of its candidate-minutes)" if not void else
                    f"{d}/'s rows make D void by bin/probe's day verdict ({'; '.join(void)}): §2 moves D to the next UTC"
                    " day, once, named in §14, and §2's **D = …**, which --draft reads, names that day")
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as root:
        with open(os.path.join(root, "v2.json"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(blob(repo, "HEAD", "prompts/v2.json") or "")
        bad = []
        for p in products:
            t = blob(repo, "HEAD", f"prompts/v2.table.{p}.json")
            if t is None:
                bad.append(f"prompts/v2.table.{p}.json is not in HEAD")
                continue
            with open(os.path.join(root, f"v2.table.{p}.json"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                fh.write(t)
            try:
                prompts.table("v2", p, root)
            except prompts.PromptError as e:
                bad.append(f"prompts/v2.table.{p}.json: {e}")
        verdict("tables", not bad, f"prompts/v2.table.<p>.json in HEAD for {', '.join(products)}, each a v2 table"
                if not bad else "; ".join(bad))
    if _git(repo, "rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", DOC_TAG, check=False).returncode != 0:
        verdict("§14", False, f"no tag {DOC_TAG}: whether {PREREG} changed since the doc tag cannot be shown")
    else:
        same = _git(repo, "diff", "--quiet", DOC_TAG, "HEAD", "--", PREREG, check=False).returncode == 0
        none = "(none yet)" in section(text, 14)
        verdict("§14", same or not none, f"{PREREG} is the doc tag's" if same else f"{PREREG} changed since the doc tag"
                + (" and §14 holds entries" if not none else " while §14 reads \"(none yet)\""))
    return fails


def since(repo, tag, products, out):
    fails = []
    r = _git(repo, "rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"{tag}^{{commit}}", check=False)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        _say(out, f"tag: FAIL: {tag} names no commit here")
        return ["tag"]
    commit = _text(r.stdout).strip()
    ok = _git(repo, "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", commit, "HEAD", check=False).returncode == 0
    _say(out, f"tag: {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'}: {tag} (commit {commit}) is {'' if ok else 'NOT '}an ancestor of HEAD")
    if not ok:
        fails.append("tag")
    _verbatim(out, f"diff: `git diff -U0 {tag}` (every tracked file as it is on disk), verbatim:",
              _text(_git(repo, *DIFF, commit, "--").stdout))
    bad = []
    for status, path in changed(repo, commit, None, ("--",)):
        v, t = VERSION_FILE.match(path), VERSION_TABLE.match(path)
        if path in SINCE_FILES or path.startswith(SINCE_DIRS):
            continue
        if (v and int(v.group(1)) >= 3) or (t and int(t.group(1)) >= 3 and t.group(2) in products):
            if status != "A":
                bad.append(f"{path}: {'removed' if status == 'D' else 'changed'} since {tag}: bin/promote only adds a "
                           f"version's files and never overwrites one, so a file {tag} holds stays as sealed")
            continue
        bad.append(f"{path}: {'added' if status == 'A' else 'removed' if status == 'D' else 'changed'} since {tag}")
    _say(out, f"allowlist: {'PASS' if not bad else 'FAIL'}: " + ("every changed path is on §13's post-seal allowlist"
          if not bad else f"{len(bad)} path(s) off §13's post-seal allowlist:"))
    for b in bad:
        _say(out, "    " + b)
    if bad:
        fails.append("allowlist")
    untracked = _text(_git(repo, "ls-files", "--others", "--exclude-standard", "-z").stdout).split("\0")
    untracked = [u for u in untracked if u]
    if untracked:
        _say(out, f"NOTE: untracked, not judged: {', '.join(untracked[:10])}" + (" ..." if len(untracked) > 10 else ""))
    return fails


def main(argv=None, repo=None, out=None):
    """`repo` exists for tests (a temporary repository); a person never has another: the tree checked is this file's."""
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="seal-check", description="PREREG-v2 section 13: the seal's checks (a)-(e), "
                                 "--draft before the draft tag, --since TAG at v2's make results")
    g = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    g.add_argument("--draft", action="store_true", help="the draft tag's preconditions")
    g.add_argument("--since", metavar="TAG", help="the post-seal allowlist from TAG to the files on disk")
    g.add_argument("--at", metavar="REV", help="the seal's verdict replayed on the commit REV names (RESULTS-v2 §0)")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    repo = REPO if repo is None else repo
    if out is None:
        out = sys.stdout
        try:                                    # PREREG text and diffs hold '§' and dashes; a C locale's stdout cannot
            out.reconfigure(errors="backslashreplace")
        except (AttributeError, ValueError):
            pass
    products = tuple(config.PRODUCTS)
    mode = "--draft" if a.draft else f"--since {a.since}" if a.since else f"--at {a.at}" if a.at else "the seal, (a)-(e)"
    try:
        head = _text(_git(repo, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout).strip()
        _say(out, f"seal-check (PREREG-v2 §13), {mode}, in {repo} at HEAD {head}, products {', '.join(products)}, "
                  f"{datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')}")
        fails = draft(repo, products, out) if a.draft else since(repo, a.since, products, out) if a.since else \
            seal(repo, products, out, a.at)
    except (GitError, OSError) as e:
        _say(out, f"seal-check: FAIL: git could not answer: {e}")
        return 2
    _say(out, f"seal-check: {'PASS' if not fails else 'FAIL'} ({mode})" + (f": {', '.join(fails)} failed" if fails else ""))
    return 1 if fails else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
